                <pb facs="0683" n="649" xml:id="pg649"/>

                <head>245. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On July 26, Secretary of State Dulles arrived in Bonn on his way to a meeting of
                    the Baghdad Pact at London July 28–31. During a 5-hour visit in the capital, he
                    discussed with Chancellor Adenauer the situation in France and the Middle East,
                    a possible summit meeting, and disarmament. Following the meeting with Adenauer,
                    Dulles met with Foreign Minister Brentano to consider nuclear weapons for
                    France, French-German relations, and a meeting of the Heads of Government of the
                    United States, the United Kingdom, France, and the Soviet Union.</p>
                <p>Memoranda of these conversations and related documentation are in Department of
                    State, Conference Files: Lot 63 D123, CF 1060 and 1064.</p>
            </div>
